 <s:String x:Key="overviewNavDescription">Connect your microphone; Veylo processes automatically. Watch your levels.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseNavDescription">Reduce background noise. Let Veylo adjust strength or choose it yourself.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="balanceNavDescription">Keep your speech at a more consistent volume.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="qualityNavDescription">Shape warmth and clarity. Compare before and after to find your sound.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="profilesNavDescription">Choose a starting sound or save your own settings.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="testNavDescription">Compare a short sample or calibrate for your microphone.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="preferencesNavDescription">Startup, keyboard shortcuts and audio engine diagnostics.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseIntro">Noise reduction aims to clean the background while preserving speech. Results depend on your microphone and surroundings.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="autoNoise">Adjust reduction strength automatically</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="autoNoiseHint">Veylo follows ambient levels between speech. It gradually increases strength in a noisier room and reduces it when the room quiets down. Speech detection helps keep your voice out of the noise estimate.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseMixHint">The manual percentage is the cleaned audio mix, not the percentage of noise removed. Automatic mode chooses between 35% and 95%.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseLive">APPLIED REDUCTION</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseLiveHint">Live strength appears while the microphone is connected. If quiet words disappear, compare a lower manual strength.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseWaiting">Waiting for microphone connection</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseBypassed">Original audio · Reduction bypassed</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="noiseDisabled">Noise reduction is off</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="automatic">Automatic</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="manual">Manual</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="balanceIntro">Slow leveling adjusts overall speech volume. The compressor softens sudden peaks. Automatic gain does not grow during silence.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="limiterHint">The final safety limiter remains active at −1 dBFS. Leveling cannot repair distortion that already occurred at the microphone input.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="qualityIntro">There is no single magic quality setting. Presets shape tone and dynamics together; use the controls below to refine the character.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="qualityQuick">Start with a voice character</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="qualityPresetHint">These buttons apply the entire preset, including noise and leveling settings. Use Profiles to save and share your own settings.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="toneTitle">Shape your tone</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="toneHint">Warmth changes lower frequencies: it can add body, but too much can sound muffled.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="clarityHint">Clarity changes speech presence. Too much can sound harsh. The advanced EQ lets you shape four frequency regions separately.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="deesserHint">The de-esser softens sharp sibilants. The high-pass filter reduces desk vibration and low rumble.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="overviewHint">With VB-CABLE, select CABLE Output as the microphone input in your application. Use Voice Quality for tone and Noise Reduction for cleaning strength.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="savedManualStrength">Manual strength (saved)</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="activeProfile">Active profile</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalTitle">Automatically tune for my voice</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalIntro">Create a starting profile for your microphone and speech levels. Get conservative recommendations for noise reduction, leveling, compression, tone and sibilance; compare before applying.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalSteps">20 seconds: 5 s silence → 7 s normal speech → 4 s softer speech → 4 s louder speech. Do not shout; repeat if the input clips.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalStart">Start the 20-second measurement</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="cancel">Cancel</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalRestoreDevice">Load this microphone’s settings</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalReady">Start the measurement when you are ready.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalPosition">Keep your microphone in its usual position. Use headphones and keep everyday sounds such as your fan running. The voice sample stays in memory.</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="personalProgress">Personal calibration progress</s:String>
 <s:String x:Key="autoAmbient">1 / 4 · Stay quiet while we measure the room</s:String>
